      "text": "```python\nfrom urllib.parse import urlsplit\n\n_ALLOWED_SCHEMES = frozenset({\"http\", \"https\"})\n_ALLOWED_DOMAIN = \"example.com\"\n\n\ndef is_allowed_url(url: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if url is an http or https URL whose host is example.com or a\n    subdomain of example.com (for example https://docs.example.com/page), otherwise False.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(url, str):\n        return False\n\n    try:\n        parts = urlsplit(url)\n        if parts.scheme.lower() not in _ALLOWED_SCHEMES:\n            return False\n        # Accessing .port validates the port and raises ValueError if malformed.\n        parts.port\n        hostname = parts.hostname\n    except ValueError:\n        return False\n\n    if not hostname:\n        return False\n\n    # Hostname is already lowercased by urllib. Allow a single trailing dot\n    # denoting the fully qualified form of the same name.\n    if hostname.endswith(\".\"):\n        hostname = hostname[:-1]\n\n    if not hostname:\n        return False\n\n    return hostname == _ALLOWED_DOMAIN or hostname.endswith(\".\" + _ALLOWED_DOMAIN)\n```",
